      "rule": "Prefer individual polity geometries over overlapping aggregate RELATIONs. Holy Roman Empire membership is shown by influence, not by merging Austria, Bavaria, Saxony, Bohemia and every small state into a modern Germany.",
      "basis": "Cliopatria distinguishes POLITY/RELATION and MemberOf. Assigning parent influence is a game adaptation."
    },
    {
      "years": [
        1648
      ],
      "rule": "Use a post-24-October snapshot and say so. Do not render every part of Alsace as French merely because France gained Habsburg Alsatian rights in 1648; Strasbourg remained outside the French kingdom in this period.",
      "basis": "Treaty wording is layered; province grid inevitably simplifies overlapping jurisdictions."
    },
    {
      "years": [
        1550
      ],
      "rule": "Delhi/Agra and the core north Indian Sur territories must be Sur. Mughal remnants in the Kabul area may remain distinct; do not erase all Mughals globally."
    },
    {
      "years": [
        1550
      ],
      "rule": "Spanish/Portuguese colonial claims do not prove actual rule over every American interior. Preserve documented Indigenous states; use named regional communities with uncertain borders for gaps, never unowned land.",
      "basis": "Contemporary Spanish maps are claims documents; LOC description explicitly says the 1562 Gutiérrez map asserted claims against rivals."
    },
    {
      "years": [
        1550
      ],
      "rule": "Japan should be described as Ashikaga shogunate / Sengoku lords if only country-wide source geometry is available. Do not falsely claim a modern unified administration; detailed daimyo borders need separate sources."
    },
    {
      "years": [
        1444,
        1648,
        1550
      ],
      "rule": "Small polities below one balanced province may be omitted, or encoded as influence if no sensible province can be assigned. Do not manufacture map dots or shift whole distant provinces only to inflate playable country count."
    }
